{title: Your Rod And Your Staff}
{subtitle: Psalms 23:4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bbmaj7] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bbmaj7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]Lord is my shepherd, I lack [Eb]nothing
He [Gm7]lets me lie down in green pas[Eb]tures
He [Gm]leads me beside still wa[F]ters
He re[Eb]stores my [F]soul so gen[Bb]tly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Even though I [Eb]walk through the [Bb]valley
Of the [Gm]shadow of death, [Bb]I fear no e[F]vil
For you are with me, [Eb]always [Bb][F]near
Your [Gm]rod and your staff, [Eb]they [F]comfort [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]You set a [F]table before [Eb]me
[Gm]In the pre[F]sence of my [Eb]enemies
[Gm]You anoint my head [F]with oil
My cup [Eb]over[F]flows with [Bb]grace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Even though I [Eb]walk through the [Bb]valley
Of [Gm]the shadow of [Bb]death, I fear no [F]evil
For you are with [Eb]me, al[Bb]ways [F]near
Your [Gm]rod and your [Eb]staff, they [F]comfort [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Goodness and [F]mercy will pur[Eb]sue me
[Gm]All the [F]days of my [Eb]life
[Gm]I will dwell [F]in the house [Eb]of the Lord
For [Bb]length of days, for length of [F]days
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Even [Eb]though I walk [Bb]through the val[Gm]ley
Of the shad[Bb]ow of death, I [F]fear no evil
For you are [Eb]with me, [Bb]always [F]near
Your [Gm]rod and your [Eb]staff, they [F]comfort [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Your rod and your [Eb]staff, they [Bb]comfort [F]me
For [Gm]you are with [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}

